message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. No scientific results or
  paper exist yet; this entry cites the research software and frozen protocol only.
type: software
title: "brats-uncertainty: reproducibility infrastructure for a pre-registered study of case-level reliability of glioma segmentation under missing MRI sequences"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/crazykush333/brain-tumor-segmentation-research"
authors:
  - family-names: Kushwaha
    given-names: Ayush
keywords:
  - brain tumour segmentation
  - missing MRI sequences
  - uncertainty
  - selective prediction
  - pre-registration
  - nnU-Net
  - BraTS
abstract: >-
  Software and reproducibility infrastructure for a pre-registered empirical
  evaluation (protocol v1.0, frozen 2026-09-28, git tag protocol-v1.0) of whether
  ensemble-disagreement confidence ranks case-level enhancing-tumour segmentation
  failures within fixed, simulated single-missing-sequence conditions. Experimental
  execution is pending; no results are included.
